menu "F*CK C5 firmware"

    config FCK_C5_FW_NAME
        string "Name this firmware greets the Kode with"
        default "c5_firmware"
        help
            The fw= of its #C5INFO line: 1 to 23 letters, digits, '_', '.' or
            '-', and anything but "fck-c5" or "c5_fck_agent", the official
            firmware's names.
            The build checks both. The Kode's SDK reads it to know this is not
            the module's own firmware (fck_firmware_t.official). Which of its
            typed calls the SDK sends is decided by the caps= of the same
            line, not by this name.

endmenu
